---
import TechniquePost from "../../layouts/TechniquePost.astro"
import BuildUpLink from "../../components/UnderTheHood/BuildUpLink.astro"
import Code from "../../components/Code.astro"
import Example from "../../components/Example/index"
import InterpolateSizeCompare from "../../components/Blog/InterpolateSizeCompare.astro"
import Basics from "../../component-examples/accordion/Basics.astro"
---

<TechniquePost slug="accordion-height-auto">
  <section>
    <h2 id="the-problem">The problem</h2>
    <p>
      A <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> element gives you an accordion for free: keyboard
      support, focus, open state and find-in-page. What it never gave you is an animation.
      It snaps open, because the content's height is <code>auto</code> and <code
        >auto</code
      > can't be interpolated.
    </p>
    <p>
      The usual fix is JavaScript that measures the content and animates a pixel
      height. Not anymore.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="the-trick">The trick</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>interpolate-size: allow-keywords</code> lets <code
          >block-size</code
        > transition to and from <code>auto</code>
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>::details-content</code> selects the part of the element that hides
        and shows
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>content-visibility</code> with <code>allow-discrete</code> keeps the
        content rendered until the closing transition ends
      </li>
    </ul>
    <Code
      lang="css"
      code={`details {
  interpolate-size: allow-keywords;
}

details::details-content {
  block-size: 0;
  overflow-block: clip;
  transition:
    block-size 0.2s,
    content-visibility 0.2s allow-discrete;
}

details[open]::details-content {
  block-size: auto;
}`}
    />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="try-it">Try it</h2>
    <p>
      The same <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> twice, with and without <code
        >interpolate-size: allow-keywords</code
      >. Open both, then slow the duration down.
    </p>
    <Example wide showCode={false}>
      <InterpolateSizeCompare />
    </Example>
    <ul>
      <li>
        With <code>allow-keywords</code> the content transitions from
        {" "}<code>0</code> to <code>auto</code> and back
      </li>
      <li>
        With <code>numeric-only</code>, the default, the same transition has
        nothing to interpolate, so the content snaps and only the opacity fades
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The real accordion. Open and close it. The content animates to its own
      height.
    </p>
    <Example column showCode={false}>
      <Basics />
    </Example>
    <BuildUpLink />
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 id="fallback">Fallback</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Browsers without <code>::details-content</code> ignore the rules and open
        instantly
      </li>
      <li>Nothing breaks, it just doesn't animate</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</TechniquePost>
